fore, the extra T6 is the least useful tile.\n\nReason: The hand is 2-shanten for Seven Pairs. The pairs B4 and J3 cannot be improved to Pungs, blocking standard hand progression. To advance the Seven Pairs hand, the player should discard the tiles least likely to form a pair. The extra T6 provides no value to the Seven Pairs structure. W3 and W7 are retained due to high availability. Between T6 and W8, T6 is the surplus of an existing pair and holds zero utility, whereas W8 has a slim chance of pairing. Thus, discarding T6 is the most efficient move.\n\nAnswer: Play T6"}
